 "note": "The Fire Station, a small bar and restaurant in the former Busselton Fire Station (No 2), 68 Queen St (west side, between the ANZ bank and Mitchell Park), built from 1936, on the City's heritage list. Not the working DFES station on Albert St (fire_station.json). From the Landgate aerial (Oct 2026), the inHerit record (brick, partly rendered and partly face-brick front, tile roof, simple rendered pilasters with chamfered edges flanking the appliance doors below a parapet) and the Busselton Mail (1930s colour scheme, courtyard on the south side facing Mitchell Park). A narrow single-storey hall about 7.7 m to the street and 20.5 m deep under a hipped terracotta tile roof, its street end a rendered parapet front with three pilasters and two wide glazed openings where the appliance doors were; the paved courtyard on the south side under four white canopy strips, and tables on the Queen St footpath. Colours, the parapet height and the lettering are guesses. Plain lettering only. Metres: x left to right as seen from Queen St (south to north), y back (west) from the front wall.",
